// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit) — FIXED, kept as regress pin
// Found by soak aug14c hz0 reactive lane (seed 4550000000 range,
// 2026-08-14, campaign binary 0b7fd7ef) ~20 minutes into the round;
// hand-reduced from the fuzzer's minimized form.
// Pre-fix: interp Trace([]; [0:i64:0]; [0:f64:0.]; [0:i64:0])
//          jit    Trace([]; [0:i64:0]; [0:f64:0.]; [])
// root_cause: the KERNEL FACE of 01/02 — sleep is PAUSE for the ride
// caches too. `impl Apply for Kernel::sleep` zeroed the interior-bottom
// taint caches (replay words, owned value pairs, per-slot reset chains)
// on the premise, true until 2026-08-14, that no fused artifact could
// sit under a sleep initiator. Arm-region fusion (Select::fuse) put a
// kernel in arm position, so a deselected-then-reselected arm returned
// to a bottomed scrutinee with NO ride history and produced nothing,
// while the node-walk rode its `Held` resident.
//
// Epoch 3 is the witness: in0=0 makes the inner scrutinee (0 % 0) %? 0
// bottom, the outer scrutinee (0 % 2 = 0) re-selects the arm slept
// during epoch 2, and the inner select must ride its cached 0.
// schedule-v1: cap=144 events=1152; in0=i64:100; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:0
{let v1 = select in0 % i64:2 {i64:0 => (select ((in0 % in0) %? in0) {i64 as n => n, _ => i64:7}), _ => f64:0.}; v1}
